course: dictionary
lesson: 7587
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «The eagle spotted its prey from high in the sky.» Here prey is an animal that is hunted and eaten.
explain: Prey can also be a verb, with the little word on. «Scammers prey on people who are trusting.» If you swap in hunt and eat, the sentence stops making sense, so prey on must mean to cheat or hurt people who are easy to trick.
explain: Ask yourself two questions: what is the sentence about, and which meaning fits it? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it works.
fact: Prey is an animal that is hunted and eaten by another animal.
fact: A predator hunts and eats other animals, called its prey.
fact: To prey on means to hunt and eat other animals, or to cheat or hurt people who are weak or easy to trick.
fact: «Eagles are big birds of prey» means they are hunting birds that catch other animals.
fact: «Fall prey to» means to become the victim of something, as in «She fell prey to a scam.»
exercise: «A predator hunts and eats other animals, called its prey.» In this sentence, what is the prey? | A hunter that catches other animals | A plant that grows in the soil | *An animal that is hunted and eaten | A place where animals sleep
exercise: «Scammers prey on people who are trusting.» What does prey on mean here? | *To cheat or hurt people who are easy to trick | To hunt and eat | To pray quietly | To run away from
exercise: In a fox and rabbit food chain, which one is the prey? | The fox | The stone | *The rabbit | The sun
test: «Cats bring prey home, and a bell on the collar can warn birds and mice.» What might the prey be? | The collar | *A mouse or a bird | The owner | The garden
test: Which phrase means a bird that hunts other animals? | *Bird of prey | Bird bath | Bird box | Bird song
exam: «Cuttlefish change their pattern, which may confuse their prey.» What are the cuttlefish trying to confuse? | The sea floor | Their owners | Their eggs | *Their prey
